🔹 Why the arrow appears
Windows adds a small arrow overlay to icons that are shortcuts.

This overlay is controlled by a registry setting, not by the icon itself.

🔹 Registry path
The setting lives under:

Code
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\Shell Icons
By default, Shell Icons doesn’t exist — you must create it.

🔹 Steps to remove the arrow
Open Registry Editor (Win+R → regedit).

Navigate to:

Code
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer
Right‑click Explorer → New → Key → name it Shell Icons.

Inside Shell Icons, create a new String Value named 29.

Set its value to:

Code
%windir%\System32\shell32.dll,-50
(This points to a blank icon resource inside shell32.dll.)

Restart Explorer or reboot your PC.

